# This deployment's FULL public URL — path prefix included. Nothing strips its
# path: every URL Vendo builds (host tool calls, login redirects, box callbacks)
# hangs off it.
#
# Dev is already done: `vendo init` asked where this app runs and wrote your
# answer to .env.local. When you DEPLOY, set VENDO_BASE_URL in your hosting
# platform's environment settings to the public URL — a production URL belongs
# in neither a committed file nor .env.local. Production fails loud without it
# (a credential-forwarding call errors instead of silently running
# unauthenticated).
#
# For reference, the dev shape:
VENDO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Optional — the host API on another origin (default: the public URL above).
# VENDO_HOST_API_URL=
# Optional — the login page (default: {public URL}/login). May be absolute,
# on another domain.
# VENDO_LOGIN_URL=
# Vendo Cloud key — REQUIRED in production. In dev, `vendo init` can mint a free starter key instead.
# VENDO_API_KEY=
# Cloudflare Access identity (see docs/authentication.md). CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN is the
# Zero Trust team name (the <team> in <team>.cloudflareaccess.com); CF_ACCESS_AUD is the
# Access application's AUD tag. Both are non-secret configuration.
# CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
# CF_ACCESS_AUD=
# Dropbox OAuth — sign-in identity for gallery editors. Create an app at
# https://www.dropbox.com/developers/apps and set these in .env.local for dev
# (or as Worker secrets for production). Register the callback URL
# http://localhost:5173/auth/dropbox/callback (dev) and
# https://manorama.xyz/auth/dropbox/callback (prod) in the Dropbox app console.
# DROPBOX_APP_KEY=
# DROPBOX_APP_SECRET=
# Signs the manorama_session cookie (HS256 JWT). Set in .env.local for dev
# and as a Worker secret for production.
# HOST_API_JWT_SECRET=
